# Smart Bulb Dashboard — environment configuration example (W2-215)
#
# Copy to `.env` in this same directory. `.env` is git-ignored and the CI
# secret scanner fails the build if one is ever committed.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. The dashboard runs with none of it set —
# this file exists for operators who would rather not keep device
# credentials in backend/config.json at all.
#
# Precedence: a variable exported in the real environment always wins over
# the value here. Docker users can skip this file entirely and pass the
# same names with `-e` / `environment:`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets --
# Move a bulb's local_key out of backend/config.json. The variable name is
# SBD_LOCAL_KEY_ + the device's `id` from config.json, uppercased, with every
# non-alphanumeric character replaced by an underscore:
#
#     config.json id "bulb-1"      -> SBD_LOCAL_KEY_BULB_1
#     config.json id "kitchen.top" -> SBD_LOCAL_KEY_KITCHEN_TOP
#
# Leave `"local_key": ""` in config.json for that device. The value below is
# used at runtime and is never written back to config.json — including when
# you rename the bulb or change any other setting through the dashboard.
#
# Sensitivity: HIGH. A local_key is permanent, unrevocable local control of
# that bulb for anyone on the same LAN. See docs/security-secrets.md.
#SBD_LOCAL_KEY_BULB_1=replace_with_your_local_key

# ------------------------------------------------------------ operational --
# Where one-click backups are written. Point it at an encrypted volume or an
# external drive. Default: backend/backups/
# Backups contain local_keys — see docs/backup-restore.md before choosing a
# synced/cloud folder here.
#SBD_BACKUP_DIR=/mnt/encrypted/bulb-backups

# Read a .env from somewhere other than the repo root.
#SBD_ENV_FILE=/etc/smart-bulb-dashboard/.env

# Per-IP login rate limit for the PIN gate (defaults: 20 attempts / 60s).
# Runtime-adjustable too, via POST /api/system/remote-auth/rate-limit.
#SBD_LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=20
#SBD_LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_S=60

# ------------------------------------------------------- NOT configurable --
# The PIN is never read from the environment: it is stored only as a
# PBKDF2 hash, set through Settings -> Remote Access.
#
# The session-signing key is never read from the environment either. It has
# to be rotatable at runtime (revoke-all-sessions rotates it), and a value
# pinned in the environment could not be rotated by the process that
# depends on it — which would quietly turn "log everyone out" into a
# partial control. See secrets_env.py.
